I need to build a To-Do List Life Dashboard that perfectly replicates the visual grid layout described below. \n\nVisual & Grid Layout Requirements:\n1. Main Background: A rich purple gradient background color (#6E57E5).\n2. Content Cards: The dashboard must consist of white rounded cards with clean drop shadows, organized using a CSS Grid:\n   - Top Card (Full Width): Displays a large digital Clock (hh:mm:ss), the full current date underneath, and a prominent dynamic Greeting text underneath the date.\n   - Middle Left Card: The 'Focus Timer' card containing a large countdown display (starting at 25:00) with 'Start', 'Stop', and 'Reset' buttons horizontally lined up below it.\n   - Middle Right Card: The 'Tasks' card containing an input text field with a placeholder 'Add a new task...', an 'Add' button next to it, and a list area below showing tasks with checkboxes and a red 'Delete' button on the right side of each item.\n   - Bottom Left Card: A 'Quick Links' card containing two inputs ('Link name' and 'URL') and an 'Add Link' button. Below the inputs, show user-added shortcut buttons (like Google, Gmail, Calendar) styled as blue pills with a little 'x' icon to delete them.\n\nTechnical Constraints:\nTC-1: Use HTML for structure, CSS for styling, and Vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks). No backend server required.\nTC-2: Use browser Local Storage API so all tasks, custom links, user greeting name, and theme settings persist safely across page refreshes.\nTC-3: Responsive layout that works smoothly across modern desktop and mobile browsers.\n\nNon-Functional Requirements:\nNFR-1 to NFR-3: Minimal, clean, user-friendly aesthetic with readable typography, fast loading speeds, and instant interactive feedback.\n\nAdditional Implemented Challenges:\n1. Custom name in greeting: Ask for the user's name via a clean input on the first visit. Save it to Local Storage and display it in the greeting text (e.g., "Good Morning, [Name]").\n2. Light / Dark mode: Place a clean toggle button inside the top greeting card that seamlessly switches the dashboard colors between a Dark mode theme and the standard Light/Purple theme.\n3. Prevent duplicate tasks: Add validation logic in the JavaScript file to stop users from adding the exact same task text twice.
